# GatewayGuard -- files kept out of version control
# The point of this repo is protecting the source of truth (the .ps1 build,
# the standards docs, the website HTML). Installers and archives are neither.

# Installers and downloads. iPrintScan-Setup is 569 MB on its own.
*.exe
*.crdownload

# Archives -- snapshots of files that are already tracked individually.
*.zip

# Preserved corruption evidence (14 MB). Kept ON DISK per DefectPrevention
# Playbook Class 7 rule 5 ("preserve the damaged file -- it is evidence"),
# but there is no value in versioning an unparseable artifact.
Tool/_corrupt/

# Python bytecode cache. Created whenever gg_edit.py is imported by a
# build_*.py pass. Regenerated on demand and machine-specific.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Windows and Office artifacts
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
~$*

# LibreOffice / OpenOffice lock files, created while a document is open
.~lock.*#

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER PUBLISH -- personal, financial and medical documents that live in
# this tree because OneDrive put them here, not because they belong to the
# product. This repository pushes to GitHub. Added 2026-08-12 so that
# committing no longer requires Bill to approve a file list he cannot be
# expected to audit.
#
# NARROW ON PURPOSE. Certificates\ and LegalZoom\ already hold 18 and 5
# TRACKED files respectively, so neither folder is ignored wholesale --
# only the specific items that must never leave this machine.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
Certificates/MaineCommunityBank/
Certificates/Banking instructions.odt

# The resurrected stale tree copy -- 803 files, its own .git inside the
# working tree. Start-CC.txt warns against starting a session in it.
Attachments/

# Screen recordings. Large, and none is a source of truth.
Videos/
